course: dictionary
lesson: 11174
title: Wingspan: a length, not a bird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wingspan is the distance from one wing tip to the other when the wings are stretched out wide. «The wandering albatross has the longest wingspan of any living bird, over three metres» tells you it is a length, measured in metres.
explain: Look at the two word parts: wing and span. A span is the distance across something. So a wingspan is how far it is from one wing tip to the other. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the bird's wingspan is about three metres" makes sense, but "the bird's wingspan is very fast" does not.
explain: Wingspan has an informal meaning too. When you stretch your arms out sideways, the distance from one fingertip to the other is your wingspan. Coaches use this to judge reach, just as scientists use wingspan to compare birds, bats, insects and aeroplanes.
fact: Wingspan is a noun: one wingspan, two wingspans.
fact: «Wingspan» means the distance from one wing tip to the other when the wings are stretched out.
fact: Wingspan is measured in centimetres or metres, because it is a length.
fact: «The wandering albatross» has a wingspan of up to about 3.5 metres, the longest of any living bird.
fact: Informal use: the distance between someone's fingertips with their arms stretched out sideways is also called their wingspan.
exercise: «The wandering albatross has the longest wingspan of any living bird.» What does wingspan mean here? | The weight of the bird | * The distance from one wing tip to the other | The number of eggs it lays | The colour of its feathers
exercise: Which unit would you use to measure a wingspan? | Litres | * Metres | Kilograms
exercise: Ella stretches her arms out wide. What does her wingspan measure? | * The distance between her fingertips | The speed of her arms | The weight of her arms | Her height
test: «Quetzalcoatlus, with a wingspan of about 10 metres, had wings of skin on one long finger.» What unit is used for its wingspan? | * Metres | Kilograms | Litres | Minutes
test: Which animal has the longest wingspan of any living bird? | Dimetrodon | * The wandering albatross | Quetzalcoatlus | Plesiosaur
exam: Jayden says wingspan only describes birds. Is he right? | No, it measures weight, not length | Yes, only birds have a wingspan | * No, it can measure bats, insects, aeroplanes and the distance between fingertips
